# Normalize line endings to LF for everything Git considers text, regardless
# of the checkout OS's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows
# checkout converts LF -> CRLF on every text file, which is silently fine for
# most files but breaks anything with a shebang that gets executed as a
# Linux/container script: `#!/bin/sh\r` is not a valid interpreter path, so
# the container exits immediately with "no such file or directory" (this bit
# docker/otel-collector/entrypoint.sh — see hyperdx-rbac-implementation-plan.md).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything invoked directly as a shell script/entrypoint inside a Linux
# container or a git hook — belt-and-suspenders on top of the blanket rule
# above, and self-documenting about *why* these specifically must stay LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
.husky/* text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf

/.yarn/releases/** binary
